  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ be a continuous function such that $f(x+1)=\\frac12f(x)$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb R$, and let $a_n=\\int_0^n f(x)\\,dx$ for all integers $n\\ge1$. Then:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}a_n$ exists and equals $\\int_0^1f(x)\\,dx$.",
    "B": "$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}a_n$ does not exist.",
    "C": "$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}a_n$ exists if and only if $\\left|\\int_0^1f(x)\\,dx\\right|<1$.",
    "D": "$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}a_n$ exists and equals $2\\int_0^1f(x)\\,dx$."
  },
